{
  "id": "wp-1787",
  "slug": "google-ai-max-ads-ai-overviews-2026-how-to-appear",
  "status": "published",
  "data": {
    "title": "AI Max and Ads in AI Overviews: How Each One Works",
    "excerpt": "AI Max for Search and ads in AI Overviews are two different Google Ads features. What each one is, where it's available and how to make your ads eligible.",
    "content": [
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Updated November 3, 2026. An earlier version of this article described AI Max as an ad format inside AI Overviews that launched in beta in February 2026. That isn't accurate: they are two different features with different dates. We rewrote it using Google's official documentation.",
            "marks": [
              "em"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "If you manage Google Ads campaigns, two names have been easy to mix up over the past year: ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "AI Max for Search",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " and ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "ads in AI Overviews",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ". One is a setting in your Search campaigns; the other is a place where your ads can show. Here's what each one is according to Google, where it's available and what to do so your ads qualify.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "The short answer",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "AI Max for Search:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " a suite of targeting and creative features you turn on inside an existing Search campaign. It isn't a new campaign type. Google introduced it on May 6, 2025.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Ads in AI Overviews:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " ads that show above, below or within the AI summaries in Search. They reached mobile users in the US in October 2024 and expanded to desktop and more countries in 2025.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "How they connect:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " AI Max is one of the ways a Search campaign becomes eligible to show within AI Overviews, alongside Performance Max, Shopping and broad match.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Availability:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " according to Google, ads within AI Overviews run in English in the US and a list of English-speaking markets.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "What AI Max for Search is",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/google-ai-max-for-search-campaigns/"
          },
          {
            "_key": "l1",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15910187?hl=en"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google introduced AI Max on May 6, 2025 as a one-click suite of targeting and creative features inside Search campaigns, rolling out in beta to all advertisers starting that month (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google, May 6, 2025",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "). The Help Center describes it as an optimization layer you activate within your existing Search campaigns and states that it is not a new campaign type (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google Ads Help: AI Max",
            "marks": [
              "l1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ").",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Its main parts, according to that page:",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Search term matching:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " uses broad match and keywordless technology (based on your assets and landing pages) to reach more searches.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Text customization:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " writes headlines and descriptions from your existing ads, landing pages and assets.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Final URL expansion:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " sends traffic to the page on your site it considers most relevant.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "And the controls to keep it in check:",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Brand inclusions and exclusions",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ", to choose which brands your ads appear alongside.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "URL exclusions",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ", so certain pages aren't used as landing pages.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Locations of interest",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " at the ad group level, based on the geographic intent of the search.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google says advertisers who activate AI Max typically see 14% more conversions or conversion value at a similar CPA or ROAS, and 27% for campaigns still running mostly exact and phrase match keywords. Those are Google's internal 2025 figures and exclude retail advertisers, so treat them as Google's claim, not as an expected result for your account. The Help page also warns that AI Max won't be effective if the campaign is limited by budget.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "What ads in AI Overviews are",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "AI Overviews are the AI-generated summaries Google shows on some searches. Ads in that space arrived in stages:",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/google-lens-ai-overviews-ads-marketers/"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "October 3, 2024:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " Google announced that ads in AI Overviews were available for mobile users in the US, above and below the overview, using existing AI-powered Search, Shopping and Performance Max campaigns, with no additional action required (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google, October 3, 2024",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ").",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/google-search-ai-brand-discovery/"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "May 21, 2025:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " Search and Shopping ads in AI Overviews expanded to desktop in the US, Google announced an English-language expansion to select countries later that year, and it started testing ads in AI Mode (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google, May 21, 2025",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ").",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/16297775?hl=en"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Today, the Google Ads Help page (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "About ads and AI Overviews",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ") sets out the rules:",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Eligible campaigns:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " Search, Shopping and Performance Max campaigns are automatically eligible. Text ads and Shopping ads can appear within AI Overviews and AI Mode.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "How keywords qualify:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " AI-powered targeting, including broad match, is eligible for both contextual matching (the query and the AI response) and direct query matching. Exact and phrase match keywords are eligible only when the query expresses direct commercial intent, not for broader exploratory questions.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Control:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " you can't target AI Overviews or AI Mode exclusively or opt out of them separately; you can use negative keywords and brand exclusions.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Measurement:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " results are included in your usual campaign metrics, and the queries that triggered ads appear in aggregate in the search terms report.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Markets:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " English, in the United States, Australia, Canada, India, Indonesia (AI Overviews only), Kenya, Malaysia, New Zealand, Nigeria, Pakistan (text ads only), the Philippines and Singapore. Google notes the list may not be exhaustive.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "How they connect (without mixing them up)",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "AI Max changes ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "how",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " your Search campaign finds queries and writes ads. AI Overviews are ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "where",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " an ad can show. The link is that a Search campaign with AI Max or broad match can compete through contextual matching inside the summaries, while a campaign with exact match only is limited to queries with direct commercial intent. Neither guarantees a placement: ads still go through the auction.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "How to prepare your campaigns",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "/en/posts/seo-2026-ai-overviews-citable-content"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Check your market and language.",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " If you advertise outside the listed English-speaking markets, ads within AI Overviews may not be available to you yet. Your organic content still matters there; see ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "how to write content AI Overviews can cite",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ".",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Test AI Max as an experiment",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " on a Search campaign with enough budget, against your current setup.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Set the controls before you switch it on:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " brand exclusions, URL exclusions and negative keywords.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Review the search terms report weekly",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " to see which queries the campaign reaches.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "/en/posts/performance-max-vs-search-2026"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Decide how AI Max fits with Performance Max:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " our ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Performance Max vs Search guide",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " covers how Google prioritizes each one.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "number",
        "level": 1
      },
